CiukiOS t23-render (real-hardware trial c42f556e, 2026-10-25). An
encyclopedia main page never appeared: 49 fetches succeeded but no remote
layout ran (remote_max_us=0).

html/object.c: box construction takes the object the parser already
fetched for the same img URL (dom_event.c html_process_inserted_img)
instead of fetching it again. Content that can reformat (SVG) and was
already READY/DONE gets those events replayed to the box callback after
the document's first layout (html.c html_box_convert_done,
html_object_ciuki_replay), as a fetch finishing later would deliver them;
its READY step sizes it from the laid-out box. With slow box construction the first fetch
completed first, llcache keeps no response to a URL with a query unless it
has an explicit expiry, and every thumbnail was downloaded and decoded
twice (18 of the trial's 49 fetches). HTML Standard, list of available
images.

html/box_construct.c: convert_xml_to_box converts elements until
CIUKI_BOX_SLICE_NS of budget time has passed, reading the clock after every
element (frontends/framebuffer/ciuki/budget.h), instead of yielding after
every 10 elements; the Ciuki main loop runs one scheduler callback per UI
turn, so a 2,300-element page cost about 230 turns before its first
layout.

